      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jiyong,\n\nI agree that it\u0027s a bit of an odd necessity to issue swapoff in the case where there isn\u0027t a backing device, but we sometimes saw that we were rebooting into flashboot if we didn\u0027t do this even without a backing device configured (we haven\u0027t root caused it yet but there was a very clear correlation between rebooting into flashboot and not issuing swapoff on the shutdown path like this even w/o a backing device). I think there\u0027s a reasonable argument to be made for not accepting this, but on the other hand in general IMO it\u0027s arguably cleaner to issue a swapoff here so as to have a predictable cleanup step on the shutdown path, and the cost to the shutdown path should be a few ms at most.",
